  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4492": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's Rugby Coach (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Welcome to the Nazareth University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Men&#39;s Rugby Coach (Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Inclusive Excellence Driving Directions Employee Benefits Human Resources Naz Homepage Assistant Men's Rugby Coach (Part-Time) Bookmark this Position Justification/Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Men's Rugby Coach (Part-Time) Position Type Staff Requisition Number ST200 Department Athletics Title of Supervisor Head Coach Rugby Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Work Hours per Week STP Weeks Per Year 40 Months Per Year: 9 Work Days Varied Work Hours Varied End Date (required for Temporary, Per Diem, Independent Contractor/Agency): Salary Range $11,600 Hours and Months Stipend Exemption Status Stipend Staff Job Description Job Description Summary The Nazareth University Assistant Men’s Rugby Coach (Part-Time) supports the Head Coach in leading our Liberty Rugby Conference at the Division I level. The Assistant Coach will have a passion for the sport and a commitment to fostering the development of student-athletes both on and off the field. Essential Functions Recruitment & Retention: Identify and recruit talented student-athletes who embody the university’s values and have the potential to succeed academically and athletically. Coaching & Development: Assist in planning and conducting team practices, providing individual and group instruction, and developing game strategies. Game-Day Preparation: Support all aspects of game-day operations, including scouting opponents, preparing game plans, and managing equipment and logistics. Team Management: Enforce team and school policies, ensuring student-athletes adhere to NCAA Division III , Empire Eight Conference (or applicable conference), and university regulations. Community Engagement: Participate in fundraising, alumni relations, and community outreach activities to promote the program. Required Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills Bachelor’s Degree Prior coaching or playing experience at the collegiate level Strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills; proficiency with technology used in recruiting and coaching Preferred Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills Master’s Degree 5+ years of coaching or playing experience at the collegiate level Advanced knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations; experience with video analysis software Supervisory Responsibilities Overseeing student-athletes or grad assistants in the absence of the head coach Physical Requirements Ability to stand for extended periods, engage in active movement, and lift equipment related to the sport Equipment to be used University vehicles Sports-specific equipment Posting Detail Information Posting Date Closing Date EEO Statement Join Nazareth University, a leading institution in Rochester, NY, with a vibrant community of approximately 1,900 undergraduate and 500 graduate students. We seek dedicated staff members who are committed to supporting student success, community engagement, and championing equity and inclusion. Located just minutes from downtown Rochester, our campus provides a dynamic environment for professional growth, innovation, and collaboration. At Nazareth, we are committed to equity and inclusion, ensuring equal access to employment opportunities without discrimination. We advocate for an inclusive workplace and welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Our Anti-Discrimination Policy upholds fair treatment based solely on qualifications and merit. Join us in celebrating diversity, where every individual, regardless of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected status, is valued and respected. Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4483 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 585-389-2065 humanresources@naz.edu Monday - Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. 4245 East Ave, Rochester, NY 14618 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4431": {
      "title": "Director of Clinical Education ~ WHNP",
      "description": "Welcome to the Nazareth University Applicant Portal Site | Director of Clinical Education ~ WHNP Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Inclusive Excellence Driving Directions Employee Benefits Human Resources Naz Homepage Director of Clinical Education ~ WHNP Bookmark this Position Justification/Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director of Clinical Education ~ WHNP Salary Range $75,000 - $95,000 Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Position Appointment Type Adminstrative Faculty Tenure Non Tenure Clinical Rank and Time Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Nazareth University Nursing Department is seeking a Director of Clinical Education at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor. The Director of Clinical Education will oversee the clinical phase of an innovative hybrid Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner Program. Essential Functions ● Oversee the ongoing recruitment, support, development, and evaluation of clinical preceptors and rotation sites for supervised clinical practice experiences ● Ensure ongoing compliance with CCNE accreditation standards and NYSED Nursing Program registration standards related to WHNP clinical education ● Responsible for the development and oversight of student assessment, to include remediation, for the clinical phase of the program ● Ensure students have met health screening and immunization requirements of assigned clinical rotation sites ● Maintain accurate student records and enforce academic policies consistent with the University, College and Program ● Ensure students are adequately prepared to achieve programmatic benchmarks and obtain NCC WHNP board certification ● Collaborate with the WHNP Program Director on ongoing assessment of student performance toward attaining the program’s Student Learning Outcomes ● Conduct and manage site visits to preceptors and students during clinical rotations ● Oversee student academic progression, retention and completion strategies ● Actively engage with programmatic evaluation ● Participate in the student recruitment, selection and admissions process ● Develop and deliver academic courses as assigned, to include curriculum development, teaching and student assessment ● Assist with curriculum evaluation and improvement ● Perform student evaluations of objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs), lab practicals, and clinical skills and procedure sessions during the didactic and clinical phases of the program ● Provide remedial instruction and reassessment as needed ● Participate in the academic counseling of students as assigned ● Serve on departmental, college and university committees as assigned ● Participate in developing, reviewing and revising the mission statement, program goals and program competencies, as necessary ● Conduct and disseminate scholarship ● Other duties as assigned Required Education, Experience, Technology and Skills ● Master’s degree, doctorate preferred ● Unencumbered WHNP license in New York State ● Prior higher education teaching experience ● Prior experience as principal faculty in a WHNP program preferred ● Effective communication and collaboration skills ● Skilled in working with a variety of different student learning styles ● Ability to perform duties autonomously with minimal supervision ● Strong computer skills ● Ability to manage and prioritize multiple tasks and successfully meet deadlines Preferred Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills ● Experience in the design, development, implementation and evaluation of clinical WHNP education ● Experience in the successful recruitment and development of clinical preceptors and rotation sites ● Experience with CCNE and NYSED standards Supervisory Responsibilities Physical Requirements Equipment to be used Special Requirements Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/11/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement 