    "https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4498": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Welcome to the Nazareth University Applicant Portal Site | Professional Writing Tutor (Part-Time Temporary) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Inclusive Excellence Driving Directions Employee Benefits Human Resources Naz Homepage Professional Writing Tutor (Part-Time Temporary) Bookmark this Position Justification/Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Professional Writing Tutor (Part-Time Temporary) Position Type Staff Requisition Number ST201 Department English & Communication Title of Supervisor Director Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Work Hours per Week 10 Weeks Per Year 40 Months Per Year: 9 Work Days Variable Work Hours Occasional Summer Hours, Temp. End Date (required for Temporary, Per Diem, Independent Contractor/Agency): Salary Range $16.00 per hour Hours and Months 10 hours per week 9 months a year Exemption Status Non-Exempt Staff Job Description Job Description Summary The Professional Writing Tutor (Part-Time Temporary) in the Charles Mills Writing Center works directly with specific student populations, as reflected by the candidate’s specialization and/or expertise. While candidates who can work with graduate students are sought, the director acknowledges support will extend beyond this singular demographic. Essential Functions Maintain regularly scheduled tutoring hours weekly. Work approximately 8 – 10 hours a week for the writing center. Attend and contribute to staff meetings. Provide additional support beyond direct tutoring (ex. handouts, workshops, content creation, etc.). Interact with students both in-person and virtually. Required Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills B.A. Degree. Exceptional recent Undergraduate candidates considered. Excellent writing and communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills. Candidate cannot be a current student at Nazareth University. Preferred Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills M.A. Degree in English or related field. Tutoring and/or teaching experience. Experience with a variety of writing tasks. Experience with specific student populations (ex. graduate students, developing learners, etc.). Supervisory Responsibilities The director might ask for minimal supervisory duties beyond contributing at staff meetings. Physical Requirements The ability to either physically work with clients in-person or to work with them virtually, synchronously or asynchronously. Equipment to be used A device to access client documents (ex. a laptop). Posting Detail Information Posting Date Closing Date EEO Statement Join Nazareth University, a leading institution in Rochester, NY, with a vibrant community of approximately 1,900 undergraduate and 500 graduate students. We seek dedicated staff members who are committed to supporting student success, community engagement, and championing equity and inclusion. Located just minutes from downtown Rochester, our campus provides a dynamic environment for professional growth, innovation, and collaboration. At Nazareth, we are committed to equity and inclusion, ensuring equal access to employment opportunities without discrimination. We advocate for an inclusive workplace and welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Our Anti-Discrimination Policy upholds fair treatment based solely on qualifications and merit. Join us in celebrating diversity, where every individual, regardless of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected status, is valued and respected. Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4486 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of Writing Work Posting Specific Questions Required fields 