    "https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4458": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Welcome to the Nazareth University Applicant Portal Site | Campus Safety Officer (C-Shift) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Inclusive Excellence Driving Directions Employee Benefits Human Resources Naz Homepage Campus Safety Officer (C-Shift) Bookmark this Position Justification/Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Campus Safety Officer (C-Shift) Position Type Staff Requisition Number ST183 Department Campus Safety Title of Supervisor Shift Supervisor Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Work Hours per Week 40 Weeks Per Year 52 Months Per Year: 12 Work Days Thursday through Monday Work Hours 11:00 p.m. - 7:00 am End Date (required for Temporary, Per Diem, Independent Contractor/Agency): Salary Range $17.75 per hour per hour (Incentives are in place to raise pay for Officers who are performing well at the 6 and 18 month marks) Hours and Months 40 hours a week, 12 months a year Exemption Status Non-Exempt Staff Job Description Job Description Summary The Campus Safety Officer (C-Shift) is an essential employee responsible for performing general and varied duty campus safety/security related work in the protection of people and property with the goal of instituting a positive culture of safety across campus. As a university authority, the Campus Safety Officer is charged with enforcement of laws (federal and state) and Nazareth University policies for all of the community. Builds and maintains positive relationships with students, faculty, staff and departments. Maintains order and promotes a positive community relations, tactful diplomacy and customer service within a Department that operates 24 hours a day and in all conditions. The Campus Safety Officer is the primary first responder to emergencies across campus including, but not limited to, fires and fire alarms, theft, vehicle accidents, missing persons, welfare checks, medical situations, mental health crisis, property damage, and injuries and accidents. The Campus Safety Officer documents all activities and situations across the University. Documentation includes narratives, witness statements, pictures, and interviews. Performs follow-up documentation and investigation at the direction of the supervisor. The Camus Safety Officer also provides general support to the department and university. Duties include, but are not limited to, door/room unlocks/locks, issuing parking citations, performing inspections of installed safety and security equipment, vehicle lockouts and jump starts. Work assignments and investigation duties involve various areas covering the entire 150 acre campus on assigned shifts. Officers must be able to act without direct supervision, and exercise independent judgment, and quick decision making handling critical situations, and emergencies that can impact the university. This position is responsible for adhering to documented Standard Operating Procedures for all functions within the position’s remit. This position is a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Clery Act. Essential Functions Patrols campus in order to observe, report, and deter suspicious and/or criminal activities, respond to emergencies, document all incidents, and take appropriate actions in line with the laws of New York State and the rules and policies of Nazareth University Responds to and initiates appropriate response procedures in line with Departmental policy for all major emergencies on campus (medical and mental health emergencies, fires/fire alarms, social unrest, auto accidents, etc.). Ensures that all campus buildings are secured and unlocked in accordance with building hours and special requests. Performs all means of assistance as needed including vehicle assists, lockouts, escorts, information requests, transports, etc.). Must complete required Daily Activity Logs, Incident Reports and associated investigations, and Building Inspection Reports, etc. Issues parking/moving violation tickets for motor vehicle infractions on campus. Ensures that all appropriate fire safety codes and regulations are properly adhered to (fire extinguisher inspections, fire drills, building inspections. Observes, reports, initiates corrective action on any hazards/defects in the buildings, roadways, walkways, or any safety or fire safety violations that may pose a security or personal threat to students, faculty, staff or visitors. Provides quality service (defined as friendly, courteous, respectful, and helpful) to students and all other members of the Nazareth University community with whom there is contact, as well as when representing Nazareth University to external organizations and individuals. Understand Campus Safety’s role in helping to promote and support the Nazareth mission of education and create a greater understanding of the department’s specific role within Nazareth. Demonstrates commitment to working in a diverse community by promoting an increased understanding of individual differences and perspectives that will enable workforce cohesiveness. High emphasis placed on professionalism, efficiency and a positive attitude. Annual participation in professional development; focuses on acquiring, improving and applying technological and other skills that are essential to achieving the goals of the university. Must be able to communicate effectively with all members of the Nazareth community, and outside emergency services. Must have a valid Driver’s License with a driving record that meets the standards set by Nazareth University’s defensive driver program and current NYS Security Guard certification/registration. Must obtain CPR / AED , emergency oxygen and first aid training certification cards within 90 days of employment. Must obtain training in Narcan, Crowd Management, Defensive Driving, and driver orientation, Bloodborne pathogens, Campus Security Authority status within 90 days of employment. Additional training requirements include accident/injury response and documentation, investigations, and response to carbon monoxide and oxygen deficient alarms. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential data, as well as high pressure emergency situations. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks, and delegate as needed. Ability to utilize good judgment to analyze situations accurately, and adopt an effective course of action. Ability to successfully manage interpersonal working relationships. Strong written and verbal communications skills. Performs other duties as assigned. Required Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills To attract a wide-ranging and diverse pool of applicants, Campus Safety prioritizes hiring based on candidates’ skill sets. This entails a focus on transferable skills and the capacity for skill development. New York State Security Guard License and Valid Driver’s License with a driving record that meets the standards set by Nazareth University’s Defensive Driver program. Preferred Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills 2 years experience in customer service, public safety or equivalent. Supervisory Responsibilities May provide oversight for one or more student workers, including graduate assistants. Physical Requirements Prolonged physical activity including time spent walking/standing in all weather conditions. Ability to patrol, walk, lift, drive and stand for extended periods of time. Equipment to be used Equipment relevant to Public Safety. Radio communication equipment, standard office equipment. Posting Detail Information Posting Date 07/07/2026 Closing Date EEO Statement Join Nazareth University, a leading institution in Rochester, NY, with a vibrant community of approximately 1,900 undergraduate and 500 graduate students. We seek dedicated staff members who are committed to supporting student success, community engagement, and championing equity and inclusion. Located just minutes from downtown Rochester, our campus provides a dynamic environment for professional growth, innovation, and collaboration. At Nazareth, we are committed to equity and inclusion, ensuring equal access to employment opportunities without discrimination. We advocate for an inclusive workplace and welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Our Anti-Discrimination Policy upholds fair treatment based solely on qualifications and merit. Join us in celebrating diversity, where every individual, regardless of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected status, is valued and respected. Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4426 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 585-389-2065 humanresources@naz.edu Monday - Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. 4245 East Ave, Rochester, NY 14618 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4491": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Welcome to the Nazareth University Applicant Portal Site | Campus Safety Communications Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Inclusive Excellence Driving Directions Employee Benefits Human Resources Naz Homepage Campus Safety Communications Officer Bookmark this Position Justification/Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Campus Safety Communications Officer Position Type Staff Requisition Number ST197 Department Campus Safety Title of Supervisor Shift Supervisor Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Work Hours per Week 16 Weeks Per Year 52 Months Per Year: 12 Work Days Saturday and Sunday Work Hours 3:00 pm - 11:00 pm End Date (required for Temporary, Per Diem, Independent Contractor/Agency): Salary Range $17.00 per hour Hours and Months 16 hours per week 12 months per year Exemption Status Non-Exempt Staff Job Description Job Description Summary The Communications Officer is an essential employee responsible for coordinating and monitoring the Campus Safety response to address calls for service and emergency situations. The Communications Officer is the primary person interacting with customers on the telephone and in-person and for documenting relevant details into the Computer Aided Dispatch system. The Communications Officer is responsible for performing support functions for the Campus Safety Department including, but not limited to, monitoring of a variety of security and fire alarm systems, issuing new and replacement NazCards, issuing controlled keys/ID cards, and processing and issuing parking permits for the entire university. The Communications Officer is responsible for managing student employees tasked with assisting communication functions. Provides general support to the entire Campus Safety Department. This position is responsible for adhering to documented Standard Operating Procedures for all functions within the position’s remit. This position is a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Clery Act. Essential Functions Coordinate and monitor Campus Safety response to address calls for service and emergency situations (Situations include telephone calls, in-person traffic, and monitored security systems) Communicate relevant information to appropriate Campus Safety (and/or emergency) personnel in a concise and timely manner. Perform intake for calls of service (telephone and in-person). Collect and document relevant information details and Campus Safety response in the Computer Added Dispatch ( CAD ) system. Provides continuous administrative support to the Campus Safety department. Assists in filing appropriate reports and forms for various walk-ups and follow-up requests. Monitors all alarm systems to include fire, security, CCTV , and the personal Safe@Naz alarm system. This includes coordinating and dispatching mutual aid emergency response with various outside agencies (police, fire, ambulance, etc.). Processes and issue parking permits for the entire campus (faculty, staff, students, and visitors). Answer and provide direction for all questions and/or concerns. Assist in troubleshoot issues with technical systems and permit billing. Monitors and operates the campus-wide Card Access system to ensure accurate data and security of the system. Creates and distributes NazCards for new members of the Nazareth Community and replace lost/damaged cards. Coordinates the updating of all campus events on a daily basis to ensure that all staff has accurate and timely information regarding special events, requests, and activities. Responsible for maintaining and issuing Campus fleet vehicle keys, specific room keys, and contractors keys/swipe cards. Maintain documentation of issuing and returning keys/cards. Provide general support to the operations of the Campus Safety Department and other duties as assigned. Required Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills To attract a wide-ranging and diverse pool of applicants, Campus Safety prioritizes candidates’ demonstrated skills, transferable experience, and capacity for continued skill development. Ability to communicate clearly and professionally by telephone, radio, in person, and in writing. Ability to remain calm, exercise sound judgment, and follow established procedures during routine and emergency situations. Ability to gather, prioritize, and accurately document information while managing multiple requests or responsibilities. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information appropriately. Ability to provide professional, responsive, and service-oriented support to students, faculty, staff, visitors, and outside agencies. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to learn and use computer-based dispatch, communication, access-control, and related departmental systems. Ability to work independently and exercise appropriate judgment within established Campus Safety procedures. Preferred Education, Experience, Technology Applications and Skills Experience in dispatching, emergency communications, public safety, security, or a related environment. Experience using computer-aided dispatch, access-control, alarm-monitoring, or similar technology systems. Experience providing customer service in a fast-paced or high-volume environment. Experience handling confidential or sensitive information. Experience working in a college, university, or other community-based setting. Supervisory Responsibilities No formal supervisory responsibilities. May provide day-to-day work direction and task coordination to student employees supporting Campus Safety communications functions. Physical Requirements Prolonged periods of sitting and computer use. Frequent movement into and out of a seated workstation while performing dispatch and customer-service responsibilities. Ability to operate telephone, radio, computer, and other communications equipment for extended periods. Essential functions may be performed with or without reasonable accommodation. Equipment to be used Multi-line telephone system Two-way radio communication equipment Computer-Aided Dispatch ( CAD ) software Alarm-monitoring and security systems CCTV monitoring systems Card-access and identification systems Parking permit and related administrative systems Standard office computer and equipment Posting Detail Information Posting Date Closing Date EEO Statement Join Nazareth University, a leading institution in Rochester, NY, with a vibrant community of approximately 1,900 undergraduate and 500 graduate students. We seek dedicated staff members who are committed to supporting student success, community engagement, and championing equity and inclusion. Located just minutes from downtown Rochester, our campus provides a dynamic environment for professional growth, innovation, and collaboration. At Nazareth, we are committed to equity and inclusion, ensuring equal access to employment opportunities without discrimination. We advocate for an inclusive workplace and welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Our Anti-Discrimination Policy upholds fair treatment based solely on qualifications and merit. Join us in celebrating diversity, where every individual, regardless of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected status, is valued and respected. Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://jobs.naz.edu/postings/4479 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 585-389-2065 humanresources@naz.edu Monday - Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. 4245 East Ave, Rochester, NY 14618 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
